  "text": "There are 60 minutes in an hour.\n\nHere is a simple summary of how solar power works: Solar panels use special materials, like silicon, to catch light from the sun. When sunlight hits these materials, it energizes tiny particles called electrons, causing them to move. This movement creates an electric current that we can use as power. By using solar energy, we can generate electricity without burning fossil fuels, which helps reduce pollution and protect the environment."
